{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HoefsmitSeminormalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HoefsmitSeminormalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_hoefsmit_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_hoefsmit_trace","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L289-L310","doc":"The figure-eight trace via Hoefsmit matrices:\n`tr(ρ_{[2,1]}(T₁ T₂⁻¹ T₁⁻¹ T₂)) = 2 - [3]_q`.  Proved\nsymbolically (SymPy, exact cancellation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_product_rho2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_product_rho2","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L235-L287","doc":"The product α·γ for axial distance 2 (the [2,1] case):\nα·γ = -1/([3]_q + 1). Key identity for the figure-eight trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_block_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_block_trace","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L211-L233","doc":"The trace of the 2×2 block equals h = q - q⁻¹.\nProved: a_ρ + a_{-ρ} = h for all ρ ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_block_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_block_det","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L119-L207","doc":"The 2×2 Hoefsmit block has determinant -1 (from the Hecke relation).\nThis is the product of eigenvalues: q · (-q⁻¹) = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitOffDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitOffDiag","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L49-L53","doc":"The off-diagonal entry as the Archimedean square root.  Used by\nthe block-determinant lemma below, where the non-negativity of the\nradicand `a·a' + 1` is established for `q > 1`, `ρ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.b_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.b_sq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.b","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitOffDiag","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L40-L47","doc":"The off-diagonal entry of the Hoefsmit seminormal form is the\nformal square root `b` of `a · a' + 1`.  Rather than\nintroducing `Real.sqrt`, we supply `b` as data and require\nthe algebraic identity `b² = a·a' + 1` as a hypothesis on the\ncaller's side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitEntry","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-seminormal-form.lean#L31-L38","doc":"The diagonal entry in the Hoefsmit seminormal form\n(axial-distance `ρ`).  Specialised to `ℝ` per §7c.  The\npositivity hypothesis `hq : q > 1` is carried for uniformity\nwith the downstream lemmas (it is not used in the body). ","signatureChunk":0}]}